    "verseCount": 6,
    "content": "<p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"1\" data-sid=\"PSA 127:1\" class=\"v\">1</span>Blessed are all they that fear the Lord: that walk in his ways.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"2\" data-sid=\"PSA 127:2\" class=\"v\">2</span>For thou shalt eat the labours of thy hands: blessed art thou, and it shall be well with thee.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"3\" data-sid=\"PSA 127:3\" class=\"v\">3</span>Thy wife as a fruitful vine, on the sides of thy house.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"4\" data-sid=\"PSA 127:4\" class=\"v\">4</span>Behold, thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the Lord.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"5\" data-sid=\"PSA 127:5\" class=\"v\">5</span>May the Lord bless thee out of Sion: and mayest thou see the good things of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"6\" data-sid=\"PSA 127:6\" class=\"v\">6</span>And mayest thou see thy children’s children, peace upon Israel.</p>",
